{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>Which Aaron made.</b> One needs to know for what purpose Scripture said this. Perhaps HaShem was insistent about the fact that they caused Aaron, the holy one of HaShem, to sin — for the sin of a great man, even if it be as thin as a hair, HaShem is exceedingly particular about it." "<b>Or</b> it may intend to remove the reproach from Aaron, for it was Israel who made the calf which Aaron made — for Aaron's deed is accounted to them, either because they forced him, or because they performed the essential act, namely the sorcery through which it emerged as a speaking [entity]."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:36:15.139462626Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}